# CODEOWNERS drives both "domain owner approval" and "merge-gate reviewer
# approval" as the SAME GitHub PR review (see DESIGN.md §3, §6).
#
# Both collaborators are listed on every rule below: whichever one isn't
# the PR author is the eligible reviewer (a PR author can never approve
# their own PR on GitHub, so this keeps every PR mergeable regardless of
# who opens it).
#
# As new IOH domains and real teams onboard, add one line per domain, e.g.:
#   /ioh/apis/payments-*   @ioh-org/payments-owners
#   /ioh/apis/logistics-*  @ioh-org/logistics-owners

# Default: any IOH-owned API not covered by a more specific rule above.
/ioh/**                    @DhanviShah23 @ridhdhisangani-spec

# All vendor submissions are reviewed by the governance team (never by the
# vendor itself — vendors are not eligible reviewers on their own PRs).
/vendor/**                 @DhanviShah23 @ridhdhisangani-spec

# Changes to CI/workflow config require the platform team.
/.github/                  @DhanviShah23 @ridhdhisangani-spec
